{"authored" [{"question" "q-42041" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x-4z=2 \\\\ 4x+y-5z=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042553/state.json" "file_sha256" "91717b101ec401919fdb69212d18af096ca13dd287dca5f5004fc2e92603b925" "basis" 1576 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042553/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-42041" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 1 & -5 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the standard Gauss-Jordan method, we can reduce this matrix to reduced row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 1 & -5 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 1 & -5 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-2z=1 \\\\ y+3z=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $y,$ and we have one free variable, $z.$ That means we need to find $x$ and $y$ in terms of $z.$ \n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=1+2z \\\\ y=-3z \\\\ z=z,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $z$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1+2z \\\\ -3z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042553/state.json" "file_sha256" "91717b101ec401919fdb69212d18af096ca13dd287dca5f5004fc2e92603b925" "basis" 1576 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042553/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-42041" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042553/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bbf8c84288812bc42555f6b12911137b4fe0e0cf7c142f3b33edf7624d0a64c3" "basis" 1576 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042553/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-42041" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042553/state.json" "file_sha256" "91717b101ec401919fdb69212d18af096ca13dd287dca5f5004fc2e92603b925" "basis" 1576 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042553/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-42041" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}-2z \\\\ 4z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042553/state.json" "file_sha256" "91717b101ec401919fdb69212d18af096ca13dd287dca5f5004fc2e92603b925" "basis" 1576 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042553/edb-import/verification.